  "solution": "<p>From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, the increasing fifth-power function gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></math>, and the increasing cube-root function gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>. Thus E is sufficient.</p><p>For contrast, A holds at (x,y)=(1,−2); B and C hold at (2,1); D and F hold at (1,−1). Each example has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>, so none of those conditions is sufficient. <strong>Answer E.</strong></p>",
